  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{M(6+3)-M(6)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(9)-M(6)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5.4-6.3}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.9}{3} \\\\  & =-0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=6$ the rate of change was approximately $-0.3$ grams per second.",
